1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:29,980
To be continued...

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:42,200
That's number 10. Isn't he amazing? Seems like he always has the ball right at his feet.

3
00:00:49,480 --> 00:00:50,440
Let's go!

4
00:00:51,120 --> 00:00:57,320
The dumb ball went to number 10 again! That raggedy-headed kid is our only problem! We need to find a way to slow him down!

5
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,600
It's...

6
00:01:05,600 --> 00:01:11,000
Talk about a hat-trick! We were down three golds, but we're tied now!

7
00:01:11,360 --> 00:01:16,080
If we keep this up, we might actually win, which will land us a spot in the prelim semifinals.

8
00:01:16,460 --> 00:01:20,280
Hard to say with how random Aoi's plays are. Watching him makes me nervous.

9
00:01:21,000 --> 00:01:23,980
He's still not paying any attention to positioning our formation.

10
00:01:24,520 --> 00:01:28,880
Who cares? Why do it if he doesn't have to? As long as he gets the gold.

11
00:01:29,420 --> 00:01:32,140
You see? We are gonna win this thing! Yes?

12
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:32,620
Yes!

13
00:01:32,620 --> 00:01:35,320
Alright! Let's go!

14
00:01:35,780 --> 00:01:37,880
Hey, Ten. Your shoe's untied.

15
00:01:37,940 --> 00:01:38,060
Huh?

16
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:40,600
Hey, it actually is!

17
00:01:40,760 --> 00:01:41,480
Aw, crap!

18
00:01:42,420 --> 00:01:44,140
Ashito, do you remember me?

19
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:44,660
Huh?

20
00:01:45,680 --> 00:01:45,940
Huh?

21
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:59,680
We were in club in grade school. Man, you were such a psycho ball hog then. No one ever really wanted you on their team because of it. Must have sucked knowing you weren't welcome anywhere. And you ended up quitting the club altogether, didn't you?

22
00:02:00,340 --> 00:02:10,000
Right! I guess it wasn't just a dream after all. But as you can see, I'm loving playing on this team now. People change. So let's make the most of the next five minutes!

23
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:16,800
Congratulations, Derrod. Glad the Podunk Junior soccer team took you on. Feel great, Mr. Big Deal in Hicksville?

24
00:02:20,240 --> 00:02:28,180
But I gotta say, the way you guys map out your plays is a snore. It's way too predictable. They pass you the ball and then go and chill over by the goal.

25
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:30,420
Least you could do is offer us a challenge.

26
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:39,540
Guess they do look like a bunch of idiots, though. All you gotta do is tell them to pass. I'm sure they think it's a great strategy every time.

27
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:46,500
You managed to get those dumb monkeys pretty well trained. Respect.

28
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:53,460
Bro! Is this a good game or what?

29
00:02:54,140 --> 00:02:58,600
I'm starting to wonder if anyone told this crowd that they're watching a junior high soccer match.

30
00:02:59,160 --> 00:03:03,240
Naiko, that's not nice. There aren't a whole lot of fun things to do in this town.

31
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:09,700
No way! He just head-butted him!

32
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:10,740
That dude is nuts!

33
00:03:10,740 --> 00:03:25,440
You told me this was your last tournament for the school year, so I took time off work to come watch you. I am such an idiot.

34
00:03:25,440 --> 00:03:30,440
Why do you go and do these kinds of things without thinking, Aoi?

35
00:03:30,440 --> 00:03:36,180
Your mother came to see you play, and yet you act like it's no big deal. And then, right in front of her eyes...

36
00:03:36,180 --> 00:03:39,180
What? You leave my mom out of it.

37
00:03:43,180 --> 00:03:52,180
I don't suppose you're aware that Coach Kijima from Dogo Business High came out to watch the game today about getting you in on a recommendation.

38
00:03:52,180 --> 00:03:59,180
He said he couldn't do it and declined. He'd heard about you and was excited about such a promising forward.

39
00:03:59,180 --> 00:04:04,180
But in the end, he said he didn't need a mentally immature player.

40
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:22,180
Ehime? What the heck brought you out there?

41
00:04:22,180 --> 00:04:24,180
The family grave.

42
00:04:24,180 --> 00:04:25,180
Huh?

43
00:04:25,180 --> 00:04:30,180
It's crazy how little things have changed. Time flows just as slowly as it always has in this place.

44
00:04:30,180 --> 00:04:34,180
Well, you really ticked nose of me off. You completely ignored the team's schedule.

45
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:37,180
Someone should check the memos, because I left full details on everything.

46
00:04:37,180 --> 00:04:39,180
Whatever! That is so not the point!

47
00:04:39,180 --> 00:04:42,180
Are you really that freaked out? It's kinda scary.

48
00:04:42,180 --> 00:04:43,180
Of course I'm freaked out!

49
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:47,180
Calm down, Hana. Now that I'm here, I'll be able to...

50
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:49,180
Get me souvenirs?

51
00:04:49,180 --> 00:04:52,180
I was gonna say there's some work here I can do.

52
00:04:52,180 --> 00:04:54,180
When? Now? Hey, I'm s...

53
00:04:59,180 --> 00:05:04,180
We're going on two hours, you know. Even a hamster would be going insane by now.

54
00:05:04,180 --> 00:05:06,180
Your legs are gonna give out.

55
00:05:09,180 --> 00:05:11,180
I'm sorry, who are you?

56
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:14,180
I've been waiting for you to stop, but you keep going.

57
00:05:14,180 --> 00:05:18,180
I don't blame you, that was quite a scene. I bet you're still pretty worked up.

58
00:05:18,180 --> 00:05:23,180
Man, you sure are something. You were already running twice as much as the other players.

59
00:05:23,180 --> 00:05:25,180
You still have the energy to come out...

60
00:05:32,180 --> 00:05:36,180
I'd like to introduce you all to our newest member. This is Ashito Howie.

61
00:05:36,180 --> 00:05:40,180
I call my position genius forward. I'm only interested in scoring.

62
00:05:40,180 --> 00:05:44,180
I'm Ronaldo in his prime, but reincarnated. I mean, he's still alive.

63
00:05:44,180 --> 00:05:48,180
But all you guys get the point. Just feed me the ball and I'll lead you to victory.

64
00:05:48,180 --> 00:05:51,180
No matter where you are, just pass it to me.

65
00:05:51,180 --> 00:05:54,180
I'm the reincarnation of Marco Van Basten, got it?

66
00:05:54,180 --> 00:05:57,180
Except Marco Van Basten's still alive too.

67
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:59,180
All right. Listen, son.

68
00:05:59,180 --> 00:06:05,180
No coach, you listen. I don't need anyone's tactics. Cause I am the tactic.

69
00:06:05,180 --> 00:06:07,180
Oh, um, well, I...

70
00:06:07,180 --> 00:06:12,180
I said I am the tactic. Know why I said it twice? Cause it's important!

71
00:06:12,180 --> 00:06:21,180
Wow, he might be the funniest guy ever!

72
00:06:21,180 --> 00:06:24,180
He's just like a goofy main character in a manga series.

73
00:06:24,180 --> 00:06:27,180
We gotta throw him a welcome party.

74
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:33,180
I can't lie about who I am. I know I'm good, so I say I'm good.

75
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:37,180
If I don't wanna do something, I'll flat out say I don't wanna.

76
00:06:37,180 --> 00:06:41,180
That's why I was always an outcast on every team I joined.

77
00:06:41,180 --> 00:06:46,180
Until then, those guys knew who I was and accepted me right from the start.

78
00:06:46,180 --> 00:06:49,180
Guess they do look like a bunch of idiots, though.

79
00:06:55,180 --> 00:07:00,180
I must have fallen asleep out here. How'd that happen?

80
00:07:00,180 --> 00:07:02,180
Huh?

81
00:07:02,180 --> 00:07:03,180
Huh?

82
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:07,180
Huh?

83
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:25,180
What? Wow! What was that?

84
00:07:25,180 --> 00:07:29,180
The time between hitting it with your chest and setting off was crazy!

85
00:07:29,180 --> 00:07:31,180
Who the heck are you, old man?

86
00:07:31,180 --> 00:07:33,180
It's just a little trick, I know.

87
00:07:33,180 --> 00:07:35,180
Want me to teach it to ya?

88
00:07:35,180 --> 00:07:39,180
With this up your sleeve, you could've scored, I'm guessing, three more goals today.

89
00:07:43,180 --> 00:07:44,180
Wanna give it a shot?

90
00:07:46,180 --> 00:07:47,180
Nope, wrong.

91
00:07:47,180 --> 00:07:51,180
Don't point your midsection toward the ball.

92
00:07:51,180 --> 00:07:56,180
When you receive it, that part of your body should already be pointed in the direction you want to run.

93
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:58,180
Huh.

94
00:07:58,180 --> 00:08:02,180
In order to maintain your field of vision, your torso twists when you make your first touch.

95
00:08:03,180 --> 00:08:05,180
And from there, you start running.

96
00:08:05,180 --> 00:08:06,180
Heads up!

97
00:08:06,180 --> 00:08:14,180
It's called control orientado. Come here, I'll show you.

98
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:23,180
Using only one touch, control the ball into one of these circles.

99
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:26,180
You have to be able to land it into any of them without missing, okay?

100
00:08:26,180 --> 00:08:28,180
Oh, and you start here.

101
00:08:28,180 --> 00:08:32,180
Once the ball's in circle, you've got three steps max to play it.

102
00:08:32,180 --> 00:08:37,180
However, you won't be able to do that unless your body's facing the right way after you make your first touch.

103
00:08:38,180 --> 00:08:40,180
Okay, got it.

104
00:08:43,180 --> 00:08:45,180
Sorry, Ashito's not home just yet.

105
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:46,180
Right.

106
00:08:47,180 --> 00:08:48,180
Where's my makeup bag?

107
00:08:49,180 --> 00:08:51,180
Crap, I'm late!

108
00:08:51,180 --> 00:08:55,180
Uh, really? What do you mean his teammates are out looking for him?

109
00:08:55,180 --> 00:08:57,180
I'm so sorry he's causing you all this trouble.

110
00:08:57,180 --> 00:08:58,180
Got it!

111
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,180
Oh, no, no.

112
00:09:00,180 --> 00:09:02,180
They volunteered to form a search party themselves.

113
00:09:03,180 --> 00:09:05,180
Unfortunately, they're coming up empty-handed.

114
00:09:05,180 --> 00:09:06,180
But they're determined.

115
00:09:06,180 --> 00:09:09,180
They only started winning games after Aoi joined the team.

116
00:09:10,180 --> 00:09:12,180
Everyone's genuinely grateful to him.

117
00:09:12,180 --> 00:09:14,180
I say just leave him out there!

118
00:09:15,180 --> 00:09:16,180
Mom.

119
00:09:16,180 --> 00:09:20,180
I took time away from my job to go watch him play and he thanks me with an act of violence?

120
00:09:21,180 --> 00:09:23,180
I don't know if I believe all that, though.

121
00:09:24,180 --> 00:09:25,180
Ashito being violent?

122
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:27,180
What reason would he have?

123
00:09:27,180 --> 00:09:29,180
Shun, I'm sorry for bringing it up.

124
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:32,180
I know how tired you are from working your own job.

125
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:34,180
Oh, it's not that bad, actually.

126
00:09:35,180 --> 00:09:37,180
Dinner's made. All you have to do is warm it up.

127
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:40,180
Make sure Ashito eats when he gets home!

128
00:09:40,180 --> 00:09:49,180
You're so bad at this.

129
00:09:49,180 --> 00:09:51,180
Know what time it is?

130
00:09:51,180 --> 00:09:52,180
It's late.

131
00:09:54,180 --> 00:09:55,180
Come on.

132
00:09:55,180 --> 00:09:57,180
I might not make check-in time at the hotel.

133
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,180
Ugh.

134
00:09:58,180 --> 00:09:59,180
Ugh.

135
00:09:59,180 --> 00:10:00,180
Ugh.

136
00:10:00,180 --> 00:10:01,180
Oh, shut up!

137
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:03,180
No one asked you to stay here all night and watch, did they?

138
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:04,180
Jeez.

139
00:10:06,180 --> 00:10:07,180
Damn it!

140
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:08,180
This is so hard!

141
00:10:09,180 --> 00:10:13,180
I can get the ball in the circle, but trying to hit it again within three steps is rough!

142
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:16,180
Maybe if I cut out all my extra movements?

143
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:18,180
Okay, time's up.

144
00:10:18,180 --> 00:10:20,180
You've gone and tried long enough.

145
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:24,180
Close control techniques might not be your thing, and that's alright.

146
00:10:25,180 --> 00:10:27,180
Guess I was expecting too much.

147
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:29,180
At this level, he probably won't make it.

148
00:10:32,180 --> 00:10:33,180
But before I go,

149
00:10:35,180 --> 00:10:37,180
I would like you to answer one question for me.

150
00:10:40,180 --> 00:10:41,180
Okay.

151
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:44,180
There was a play you made today that I found truly spectacular.

152
00:10:46,180 --> 00:10:49,180
Your team's one yen coins.

153
00:10:50,180 --> 00:10:51,180
Ten yens are the opposition.

154
00:10:52,180 --> 00:10:55,180
We're looking at when you scored right before you were set off.

155
00:10:59,180 --> 00:11:01,180
You were here when you suddenly changed direction.

156
00:11:02,180 --> 00:11:04,180
Then, you picked up the loose ball that dropped right here,

157
00:11:05,180 --> 00:11:08,180
and then somehow squeezed your shot through these defenders to score.

158
00:11:10,180 --> 00:11:12,180
What are you? Some kind of stalker?

159
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:14,180
You aren't really interested in tactics, are you?

160
00:11:14,180 --> 00:11:17,180
All you care about is just scoring and scoring.

161
00:11:17,180 --> 00:11:19,180
You run wild and hope it happens.

162
00:11:20,180 --> 00:11:22,180
You can't play the game without your teammates.

163
00:11:23,180 --> 00:11:24,180
Unless you want to be a jerk player.

164
00:11:24,180 --> 00:11:25,180
You're a jerk player.

165
00:11:27,180 --> 00:11:28,180
And yet...

166
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:33,180
Seems like no matter what, the ball comes to you.

167
00:11:34,180 --> 00:11:35,180
Oh!

168
00:11:36,180 --> 00:11:37,180
Damn it!

169
00:11:37,180 --> 00:11:38,180
For the entire match.

170
00:11:39,180 --> 00:11:40,180
Crazy.

171
00:11:41,180 --> 00:11:42,180
It's like the ball's drawn to you.

172
00:11:43,180 --> 00:11:45,180
It looks for the guy who plays without thinking.

173
00:11:46,180 --> 00:11:49,180
That's why it seemed like you were the only one on the field.

174
00:11:50,180 --> 00:11:54,180
Your teammates trust you completely and will always pass to you no matter what.

175
00:11:54,180 --> 00:11:55,180
It feels natural to them.

176
00:11:56,180 --> 00:11:57,180
But...

177
00:11:58,180 --> 00:11:59,180
All their skill levels are pretty low.

178
00:12:00,180 --> 00:12:05,180
So most of your opportunities to score came from the incredible number of loose balls you picked up.

179
00:12:06,180 --> 00:12:07,180
Were you aware of any of that?

180
00:12:08,180 --> 00:12:09,180
Can't you see I'm trying to concentrate?

181
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:11,180
Quit your yapping!

182
00:12:12,180 --> 00:12:13,180
Wow, you're scary!

183
00:12:17,180 --> 00:12:20,180
He had been acting really strange since the game ended this afternoon.

184
00:12:21,180 --> 00:12:24,180
When we asked him what was wrong, he said he wanted to come here and apologize.

185
00:12:25,180 --> 00:12:27,180
I'm not proud of this, but...

186
00:12:28,180 --> 00:12:32,180
When we were at the game, I talked some smack about Aoi's team.

187
00:12:33,180 --> 00:12:37,180
But I... I didn't mean it. I was just trying to throw him off a bit.

188
00:12:37,180 --> 00:12:41,180
He seemed fine. Just took it all in and didn't react much.

189
00:12:42,180 --> 00:12:44,180
I did it because he was always on the ball.

190
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:47,180
I thought we'd never win while he was on the field.

191
00:12:48,180 --> 00:12:50,180
I was trying to make him hit me!

192
00:12:51,180 --> 00:12:54,180
Guess your mom finally saved up enough change to buy you some real gear.

193
00:12:55,180 --> 00:12:58,180
Man, remember how you used to be crazy poor?

194
00:12:59,180 --> 00:13:00,180
Oh wait, I take it back.

195
00:13:01,180 --> 00:13:03,180
Looking at those cleats, it's obvious nothing's changed.

196
00:13:04,180 --> 00:13:05,180
Dude, it was so awkward.

197
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:07,180
Everyone was so embarrassed to play with you.

198
00:13:08,180 --> 00:13:10,180
Since your mom worked the quote-unquote night shift.

199
00:13:15,180 --> 00:13:17,180
If you wanna fight me, then fight me!

200
00:13:18,180 --> 00:13:19,180
Call me any stupid thing you want!

201
00:13:19,180 --> 00:13:20,180
I don't care, jerk!

202
00:13:21,180 --> 00:13:23,180
I suck, I'm ugly, I'm a brainless idiot!

203
00:13:24,180 --> 00:13:25,180
Whatever you got, throw it at me, man!

204
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,180
But leave my mom out of this!

205
00:13:28,180 --> 00:13:29,180
Leave her out of it, do you hear me?

206
00:13:32,180 --> 00:13:33,180
I'm so sorry!

207
00:13:33,180 --> 00:13:34,180
We won the game!

208
00:13:35,180 --> 00:13:37,180
But I felt so guilty about what happened, I didn't care!

209
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:39,180
I'm sorry!

210
00:13:40,180 --> 00:13:41,180
I'm sorry!

211
00:13:42,180 --> 00:13:43,180
You okay?

212
00:13:43,180 --> 00:13:44,180
The last goal I made?

213
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:53,180
Well, yeah, if you only look at what was up in the area around the goal, you might be right.

214
00:13:54,180 --> 00:13:57,180
But we spread all my teammates out like this for a reason.

215
00:13:58,180 --> 00:13:59,180
Because they were all tired.

216
00:14:00,180 --> 00:14:02,180
And because the other team's formation was neat and tight.

217
00:14:02,180 --> 00:14:06,180
So I figured if I hung out in this space, I could move around however I wanted.

218
00:14:07,180 --> 00:14:10,180
And worst case, I could react to any counterattack they made.

219
00:14:11,180 --> 00:14:13,180
That's when I got the ball which led to me scoring.

220
00:14:14,180 --> 00:14:16,180
A genius play by a genius player.

221
00:14:16,180 --> 00:14:21,180
But I guess if I'm being honest, it's all thanks to my teammates who got the ball to me even though they were exhausted.

222
00:14:22,180 --> 00:14:23,180
They're great!

223
00:14:24,180 --> 00:14:25,180
So you see, it really wasn't a loose ball at all!

224
00:14:26,180 --> 00:14:27,180
It wasn't a coincidence!

225
00:14:28,180 --> 00:14:29,180
It was a team goal!

226
00:14:29,180 --> 00:14:38,180
I've got a short fuse.

227
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:42,180
I can't do anything unless they let me play the way I want to on the field.

228
00:14:43,180 --> 00:14:45,180
The only thing I think about is what I'm gonna do next.

229
00:14:46,180 --> 00:14:49,180
And these guys, they were the first to accept me as I am.

230
00:14:50,180 --> 00:14:53,180
They reminded me why I've stuck with this sport for so long.

231
00:14:53,180 --> 00:14:59,180
I love playing soccer.

232
00:15:01,180 --> 00:15:03,180
Anyway, that's the way it works with us.

233
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:05,180
And I like it.

234
00:15:08,180 --> 00:15:09,180
Huh?

235
00:15:12,180 --> 00:15:14,180
What's going on with you, old geezer?

236
00:15:15,180 --> 00:15:17,180
You're starting to creep me out.

237
00:15:20,180 --> 00:15:22,180
Hey, where are you going?

238
00:15:23,180 --> 00:15:24,180
I need to chill for a bit.

239
00:15:25,180 --> 00:15:26,180
You should go home.

240
00:15:33,180 --> 00:15:34,180
Unbelievable!

241
00:15:35,180 --> 00:15:36,180
Every single one of them?

242
00:15:37,180 --> 00:15:38,180
That's insane.

243
00:15:39,180 --> 00:15:43,180
How could that kid possibly remember the positions of all 22 players on the field?

244
00:15:53,180 --> 00:16:09,180
I just fell asleep out here like some backpacker.

245
00:16:09,180 --> 00:16:10,180
Huh?

246
00:16:23,180 --> 00:16:25,180
There's no way. He's been at it all night.

247
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:35,180
Oh, you're up! It worked! It all started to click around dawn and I've been unstoppable! I'm even better now!

248
00:16:35,180 --> 00:16:44,180
You're one creepy little kid.

249
00:16:44,180 --> 00:16:45,180
I'm the manager of Tokyo City Asperion FC Youth, Tatsuya Fukuda.

250
00:16:45,180 --> 00:16:46,180
Oh, okay.

251
00:16:46,180 --> 00:17:02,180
Every J League team has a youth team made up of high school aged players. I have an ambition, you see. I want to have the world in the palm of my hand with a perfect team I've put together. And it won't just be a step to the stage. Our club is going to become the world.

252
00:17:02,180 --> 00:17:31,180
stage. Barca, Madrid, Manchester, Milan will crush them all. And the thing that's going to make it all possible is the youth team. Come to our tryouts. They're going to be held in Tokyo.

253
00:17:32,180 --> 00:17:39,180
Ten days from now. When you get home, be sure to discuss it with your family.

254
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:09,180
I knew it! That is Ashito! Hey, you have been out here practicing every day lately!

255
00:18:09,180 --> 00:18:16,180
It's too bad about the tournament, but we had a good time rooting for you. We both forgot we had instruments in our hands a few times.

256
00:18:16,180 --> 00:18:23,180
Yeah, but what about high school? Does that mean you missed out on that recommendation?

257
00:18:23,180 --> 00:18:30,180
I'm not worried about it. I can still play soccer wherever I go.

258
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:31,180
Hi there, new team! Good job!

259
00:18:31,180 --> 00:18:32,180
Yeah, thanks!

260
00:18:32,180 --> 00:18:37,180
Oh! Hey! What's up, Ashito? May as well play a game with these guys since we came all the way out here, right?

261
00:18:37,180 --> 00:18:44,180
Yeah! Let's do it!

262
00:18:44,180 --> 00:18:45,180
Cheers!

263
00:18:45,180 --> 00:18:46,180
Oh!

264
00:18:46,180 --> 00:18:49,180
Hi there, new team! Good job!

265
00:18:49,180 --> 00:18:50,180
Yeah, thanks.

266
00:18:50,180 --> 00:18:53,180
Oh, hey! What's up, Ashito?

267
00:18:53,180 --> 00:18:57,180
May as well play a game with these guys since we came all the way out here, right?

268
00:18:57,180 --> 00:18:59,180
Yeah! Let's do it!

269
00:19:13,180 --> 00:19:15,180
Check out Ashito.

270
00:19:16,180 --> 00:19:18,180
These really got better, don't you think?

271
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:25,180
An invitation from a youth team in Tokyo.

272
00:19:25,180 --> 00:19:30,180
What the heck are you babbling on about? I'm not sending you off to Tokyo alone!

273
00:19:30,180 --> 00:19:32,180
How old do you think you are?

274
00:19:32,180 --> 00:19:33,180
Easy.

275
00:19:33,180 --> 00:19:37,180
You're still in junior high. You wanna just leave and play soccer?

276
00:19:37,180 --> 00:19:40,180
Don't you know what we're going through right now?

277
00:19:40,180 --> 00:19:45,180
That costs money, and we don't have much.

278
00:19:45,180 --> 00:19:50,180
That sucks. I'm sorry your recommendation fell through.

279
00:19:50,180 --> 00:19:55,180
So what? You're going to Fatami High then, right?

280
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:58,180
Quit the rest of us? That's so great.

281
00:19:58,180 --> 00:20:07,180
Now just think, if we win, we'll set a record. Weakest team to ever go to nationals!

282
00:20:07,180 --> 00:20:12,180
Yeah. Yeah, you're right. It's a good goal.

283
00:20:12,180 --> 00:20:17,180
Huh? Huh. Hey, Shun.

284
00:20:17,180 --> 00:20:18,180
Shun?

285
00:20:18,180 --> 00:20:20,180
You've been coming home pretty late these days.

286
00:20:20,180 --> 00:20:23,180
And since then I didn't have to go into work today, I thought I'd come pick you up.

287
00:20:23,180 --> 00:20:32,180
Tatsuya Fukuda. He's an ex-midfielder who used to play for the national team.

288
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:37,180
That guy who gave you that invitation. He's actually a legendary player.

289
00:20:37,180 --> 00:20:38,180
Really?

290
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:44,180
He's from Ehime Prefecture. From what I read. But his family moved away when he was in grade school.

291
00:20:44,180 --> 00:20:51,180
He hasn't played a single game for well over ten years at least. So it's no wonder you've never heard of him.

292
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:59,180
After graduating from a big-name school known for soccer, he joined J1's Tokyo City Espirion at age 18.

293
00:20:59,180 --> 00:21:06,180
Then he was promoted to starter by age 20. He hit his prime at age 23. That's when he went to play in La Liga, Spain.

294
00:21:06,180 --> 00:21:08,180
You know, the best league in the world.

295
00:21:08,180 --> 00:21:10,180
In Spain?!

296
00:21:10,180 --> 00:21:15,180
He was a genius who bloomed early. The whole world knew who he was.

297
00:21:15,180 --> 00:21:19,180
And that is where my knowledge of his history gets foggy.

298
00:21:19,180 --> 00:21:24,180
From what I can remember, he suffered a serious injury in the final game of that last season.

299
00:21:24,180 --> 00:21:30,180
He did make a comeback, but he never hit the same heights. He must have retired not long after.

300
00:21:30,180 --> 00:21:34,180
I had no idea he became a youth team coach, though.

301
00:21:34,180 --> 00:21:47,180
Ever since that day, I just... I haven't been able to get my heart to stop racing. I have no idea what that means.

302
00:21:47,180 --> 00:21:56,180
Some random guy gives me pointers out of the blue, and I can't get his words out of my head no matter how hard I try.

303
00:21:56,180 --> 00:22:06,180
You should go. At least try out. We'll deal with whatever happens after that as it comes. Here, take this with you.

304
00:22:09,180 --> 00:22:19,180
It took me a while to save up that much. So don't waste it, okay? I'll talk to Mom. Don't worry. Something's out there for you. So go find it.

305
00:22:19,180 --> 00:22:32,180
Come to our try outs. I'll take you to the world stage.

306
00:22:32,180 --> 00:22:33,180
Bye.

307
00:22:33,180 --> 00:22:34,180
Bye.

308
00:22:34,180 --> 00:22:35,180
Bye, bye, bye.

309
00:22:35,180 --> 00:22:36,180
Bye.

310
00:24:05,986 --> 00:24:28,986
Next time on Al Ashi, Tokyo City Espirion!

